WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Yo-Noid, or How a Yo-Yo Saved New York.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:28.420
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.060
I'm Mike. And I'm Sean.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.600
Yo, Mike. Yeah, yo, Sean.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.160
What's up? How you doing?

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.280
You think that the Yo is mandatory as part of the Noid?

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.840
I think with, like, you know, early 90s, Yo is mandatory.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:54.200
Maybe not so much in relation to Noid himself, but I think, like, I was expecting more titles like this.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.760
What do you know about the Noid?

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.800
I didn't know a goddamn thing until this episode came on our radar.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:01.960
And so-

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.660
Now I feel like it, this is some, like, Mandela effect thing.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:08.840
Yeah. No, I knew about the Noid because he's, like, an-

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.940
He's an annoying, obnoxious character.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.200
But here's my whole, here's my, like, get into it real early in the episode.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.500
So, like, McDonald's has the Hamburglar, right?

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.420
And, like, he wants to steal-

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.900
And Ronald McDonald and so many others.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.680
Yeah, yeah. So many other mascots.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:34.680
But I'm bringing up the Hamburglar specifically because he wants to, like, steal the Big Mac because it's delicious.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:35.980
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:45.060
So you mean, like- Yeah. You're talking about the built-in villains and antagonists of your marketing campaign.

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:58.020
Right, right, right, right. But, like, even though the Hamburglar is, first off, like, a 10 out of 10 name, one of the best marketing gimmicks of all time, but, like, he still loves the McDonald's burger.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.860
He's not stealing the burgers because he secretly works for Burger King and hates McDonald's.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.300
The Noid hates Domino's.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.520
Like, it's really strange, right?

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:22.600
Yeah, I guess it's more so just an agent of chaos than it is anybody that has an opinion on the food from what I was able to gather.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.960
Yes, he's not- But then again, I didn't really do that much gathering.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.700
He's not a real entity.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:36.480
He's, like, what could go wrong to make your delivery not be delivered in time because Domino's was, like, 30 minutes or less, you know?

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.080
And so it's like- So he's Michael Madsen.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:44.220
Yes. And the Noid would make you annoyed, right?

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.220
Like, it's insufferable.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.880
So I guess that's the Noid part of it is he's called that because-

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.280
I thought it would be, like, the paranoia.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.740
I guess I don't really know.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.100
I think it's for annoyed, if you want me to be honest.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.540
I don't have, like, a citation for that.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:07.880
I think he stands for, in our society, certain patterns, you know?

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:13.600
And NOI, like, sort of like a return on investment.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.580
Got it.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.360
There's a CBS cartoon about the Noid.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.380
I don't think it ever saw the light of day.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:51.460
I couldn't find, like, a pilot for it or anything, but it was planned.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:55.340
And then there's actual, like, Domino's merchandise with the Noid.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.280
So- Do we know why he was a rabbit?

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.540
Why he wears those ears?

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.800
Oh, he just wears the ears.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.180
Do we know that if he pulled them off that he would have giant bunny ears?

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:08.240
Or do we just assume-

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.900
I guess I don't know. I thought maybe that was just his skin.

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:14.920
And I think it's just, like, again, because he's supposed to just be irritating to look at.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:26.520
Yeah. Now, in 1989, a Georgia man named Kenneth Lamar did hold two Domino's employees hostage.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.280
His name was Noid.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:29.420
Yeah. Sorry.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:30.400
I left out the-

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.760
I was saving that for the punchline.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:36.220
But, like, his name was Kenneth Lamar Noid.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.020
And he held two Domino's employees hostage.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.420
He surrendered eventually.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.840
Nobody was hurt or anything.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:47.040
And there is a conspiracy that this is what got the Noid off the air.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.880
Well, I did also find this out.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:56.660
Which I, again, part of why I thought this was some kind of, like, Mandela effect situation.

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:58.360
Because it's like, I would have-

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.040
I feel like I would have known about this.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.420
But apparently I didn't.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:08.220
And also, I think, like, they only retired the Noid, like, five years after this.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.440
So, it doesn't hold that much water.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:17.020
I think hopefully maybe in the 90s people were just like, this has been weird the whole time.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.040
And we've just kind of had enough of it.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:24.080
But one thing I want to push back on is you've-

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.280
You've said that he surrendered.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:37.280
Whereas the story that I read goes that he was sort of outsmarted by his captors who made him pizza.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.040
And then he, like, put the gun down and they just ran away.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.680
So, he surrendered to the pizza.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:48.920
Yes. He surrendered to his cravings for Domino's.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:53.940
Which, if you ask me, sounds like some pretty awesome marketing for your pizza.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:06:03.260
If, like, even would-be hostage takers can't really-

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:05.660
Can't say no to the taste.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.900
But I just missed opportunities.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:11.400
Where they were getting briefed on it, you know, like, up at Domino's HQ.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.560
And they were like, you know, please don't die.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:17.160
Please don't die. And then they heard that the pizza was so good that he surrendered.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:19.720
And they were like, we got to do something about this.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.700
The Noid did come back, though, a few times.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.540
2011 for the 25th birthday.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:33.000
He got, like, a Facebook video game, web game, called Noid's Super Pizza Shootout.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.200
Whoa. Yeah.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.420
That's a little strange considering.

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:39.600
Close to the hostage incident.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.700
And then in 2016, Domino's got a pinball machine.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:44.960
And the Noid's in it.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.780
Like, it's not, like, all about him, but he's in it.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.660
And so, like, another reference to him.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.680
But for the most part, like, I don't know.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:07:01.140
Domino's has had long enough time away from him that I don't think anyone other than the people who grew up with the Noid associate the two together.

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:02.920
I sure as hell didn't.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:11.200
Right. But I guess just a question a little further outside the scope of the video game in front of us.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.680
Do you like Domino's pizza?

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.140
Okay. So this is a great question.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.340
And it is one I planned to answer.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:18.820
So I have a good response here.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:28.680
And for the longest time, especially growing up on Long Island and going into the city, like, that's where the best pizza in the world is.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:36.060
And I never saw a need to have the Domino's, Papa John's, Pizza Hut, Little Cece's, whatever.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.320
Whatever there is out there.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.120
I didn't feel the need to ever.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.420
Little Caesars. Little Caesars and Cece's pizza, right?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.680
Yeah. I combined them.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.760
There was never a need for that in my life.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:52.780
But my wife does, I would say, love Domino's.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.080
So I had to, like, have it, obviously.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.140
Like, it's in my life now.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.820
There's actually, like, a yearly tradition around Christmas time where I give her, like, a Domino's gift card and we have it.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:09.080
And the first time I had it, I have to say I was surprised that it's not really pizza.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:10.440
It's Domino's.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.500
It's not the same kind.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:16.100
It doesn't satisfy the same way a thin New York slice does.

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:23.080
This is, they've kind of, like, carved out their own area of the pizza market where it's like, I get it.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:27.680
If you're going to Domino's, you don't want that, like, thin crust slice.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:32.360
Yeah, you want Domino's. And so I am not a Domino's hater any longer.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:33.640
Well, I'm glad to hear that.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:40.320
I also think that Domino's has its place alongside, you know, I think pizza has its own thing,

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:43.120
too. And they all have a purpose.

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:46.300
Now, I do want to bring up another thing about Domino's.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:50.600
And maybe you can help me with this or maybe you'll just come to the same conclusion I did.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:58.680
But since I've been eating Domino's, which is probably right around 2014, there has been a deal on the website

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:06.720
where for $20 you get two medium pies, like the garlic knots or whatever they call them.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:09.020
It's because they're not knots. Cheesy bread. No, no, no.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.660
It's like, it's definitely garlic something.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.940
It's like garlic twists. There's garlic Parmesan twists.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:23.160
Okay. And then you get cinnamon twists, too, with like a cheesecake dipping sauce or whatever, and a two-liter bottle of Coke.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:24.540
And now that's all for $20.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:30.260
Okay. They eventually get rid of the two-liter bottle of Coke, and it's still the $20.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:35.000
There's no other promo on that site that even comes close.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:41.940
Like, you might not even be hungry for the whole thing, but for the price difference, I've tried every other combo you can think of.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:42.960
I've tried their other coupons.

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:49.340
There's no reason not to just get two medium pizzas, the garlic thing and the cinnamon thing, and just call it a night.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:52.920
Yeah, that's probably something like 4,000, 5,000 calories right there.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:55.700
Yeah, but again, if you're having it at 2 a.m., it don't count.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.920
You have said this.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.100
Offline, I've said this, yeah.

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:08.620
I'm just thinking about, like, the price per calorie or calories per dollar, you know?

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:10.180
So that is the deal.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.160
That is a deal right there.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.920
You asked why he looks like that.

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:16.020
I do want to know that.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:17.220
I'm going to put that in your words.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:25.280
Apparently, the red suit with the rabbit-like ears and the big N just read well in claymation.

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:33.260
So they gave him the ears because it made him pop more on older TV sets.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.920
That's the alleged citation that I have here.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.360
I'm not going to investigate the source.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:39.460
But I guess that makes sense, right?

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:44.900
Like, if he just had, like, a red cap, it wouldn't stand out that much.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.600
Like, he needed a little something extra to mascot him.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:11:00.680
Now, you know, one thing that doesn't particularly read well, and I'm going to loop this into the game itself here, too, is the association with Domino's Pizza.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:12.420
Because, I mean, again, I guess it's part of his whole, like, antagonistic streak that, you know, he does, he's not, he's not the, he isn't representing Domino's.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.060
He's representing what could go wrong in a Domino's delivery.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:26.080
But even, like, in this game, like, the pizza is, the pizza place that you go to over and over, it doesn't happen to be Domino's.

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.040
It's just a pizza place.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:34.640
Like, it's just, this is a Noid game, and the whole association with Domino's is very much incidental, it seems.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:42.340
And yet it is kind of funny that every level ends with him being forced to have a pizza-eating competition, something he hates.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:53.340
He hates pizza, and he and the other Noids that live in this Noid land have to eat pizza, and whoever eats the most moves on to the next round.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:57.000
There is something poetic about that.

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:00.180
Very. I'm not sure what kind of poetry it is.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:06.200
It's, like, more, maybe it's more, like, slam poetry without rhyming.

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:08.960
But, you know, it's poetry.

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:17.380
Sean, can a licensed mascot platformer ever earn a seat next to Capcom's original NES greats, like Mega Man?

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:19.120
Like, is there ever a chance?

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.680
Like, the quality of this video game?

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:30.200
Not the quality of this video game specifically, but I guess, like, does, so they're creating, like, their own mascots, Capcom, right?

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:35.580
Like, they are making games with great, memorable IPs that are still being made today.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:40.580
And then, like, they're also making licensed games at the same time.

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:47.600
And it's, like, do you have a certain judgment about the quality of these just knowing that it's a Domino's tie-in because of the other?

00:12:47.720 --> 00:13:01.020
Like, we are basically, at this point in the show right now in the 1990s, we have become, like, a pop culture podcast because everything is a licensed, like, movie or toy or franchise of some sort.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:11.700
And, you know, I guess, like, I'm not saying I had a bias going into it, but I certainly didn't expect this to be on the level of Capcom games because of the forced tie-in.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:25.140
Yeah, I think that the only reason that the last episode that I can think of that even comes close to this would be the spot game.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:29.620
And I'm pretty sure we also had, like, a McDonald's one, but that...

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:30.920
We did. We did.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:33.980
Okay. Um, but I had...

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:43.940
I had... Myself had nostalgia for a spot video game, so I think that kind of disqualifies me from having an actual opinion on the game itself.

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:47.680
But, like, on the quality of any other spot video game.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.640
But, like, this one...

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:59.740
Having not known what Noid was and then learning that it's Domino's Pizza, I think I did have some prejudice against it as, like,

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:01.040
Oh, this is gonna be a good game.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:02.800
Obviously, it has to.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.580
It's Domino's Pizza, right?

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:05.880
No one's gonna think that.

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:09.780
And Capcom basically took a game that they had already made.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:15.740
I don't know how to say it in Japanese, so it just translates to Masked Ninja Hanamoru.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.560
And that game just...

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:25.640
It's basically the same game, but it got a complete visual overhaul to fit the Noid and the pizza and all that into it.

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:32.540
But it wasn't like they started from scratch, like, coming up with a Yo-Noid video game.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.020
They basically looked at what they had and then said, like...

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.900
I guess, like, they probably went to Domino's or somebody and was like,

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.580
Who wants to make a game with us?

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:41.800
And who wants to pay us money?

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:43.420
And Domino's was like, us!

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:46.460
And then they were like, but did you remember to include our logo anywhere?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.520
Wow, you actually just kind of creeped me out.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:54.300
Because I was wondering why you kept using Capcom as an example of just like,

00:14:54.300 --> 00:15:01.780
Oh, you mean like, maybe this is a little Mega Man-y, so this is why Mike is bringing it up as a comparison.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:04.400
Like, no, Capcom made this game.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:06.340
That's actually...

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:13.900
And I remember now seeing this on the intro screen and it just completely washing over me.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:18.020
It's actually crazy that they made this game.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:25.560
Yeah, now what I understand is that they played a role in the making of this game and were definitely the publisher of the game.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:33.320
Seems like now Productions might have made the, like, original Japanese game, the Mass Ninja one.

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:35.740
And then Capcom just, like, re-skinned it here.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.400
So it's not a true...

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:42.280
I mean, it is technically a true Capcom game because it's under their, like, wing.

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:43.500
Yeah, they're umbrella, yeah.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:48.100
In these times, it probably means more to be the publisher than the developer of these games, right?

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:52.000
Because you're, like, you're riding your new face on all this, right?

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:54.540
It's your reputation at stake.

00:15:54.860 --> 00:16:00.740
Yeah. So all that in mind, the game aspect of it all, right?

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:06.700
It's a Capcom-published, side-scrolling platformer starring the Domino's mascot.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:10.040
But, like, what are we in for here, Sean?

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:18.480
Is this actually anything more than a shameless advertisement game?

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:23.020
It definitely is not because there's so little advertising.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:24.740
I think there are really...

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:34.140
The assumption here was that Noid is such a cultural phenomena in itself that it's a...

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:36.580
Like, that it sort of stands on its own.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:44.620
Because, again, like we were mentioning, I don't remember seeing any Domino's branding aside from on the...

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:47.620
Like, on one of the, like, credit screens.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:56.900
Because other than, like, each level ending in that pizza contest, there really isn't much going on here.

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:58.280
He's more...

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:05.080
I would have thought, without any other context, that he was the mascot of a yo-yo company.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:07.120
Because I don't know where the yo-yo came from.

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:08.880
Did he have a yo-yo in the commercials?

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:12.720
I don't know. Isn't it the yo-yo because it's yo-noid?

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:15.880
Yo-noid? But, like, that's just, like...

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.700
That's not from anything.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:19.080
That's just...

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:23.180
What if you gave the Hamburglar a cello?

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:24.800
Like, and then he...

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:28.000
That's just what he... That was just what he played in, like, a music rhythm game.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:29.260
Like, is that...

