I, too, agree that they should have

00:30:48.020 --> 00:30:50.180
painstakingly added the string

00:30:50.180 --> 00:30:51.780
during attack animations.

00:30:51.780 --> 00:30:53.640
But what they do have,

00:30:54.180 --> 00:30:55.340
it still has, like,

00:30:55.380 --> 00:30:57.140
it still feels like a yo-yo to me.

00:30:57.140 --> 00:30:59.800
I didn't read it as Magic Baseball.

00:31:00.840 --> 00:31:02.520
I think that, you know,

00:31:03.080 --> 00:31:06.320
I'm not going to defend this all that wholeheartedly

00:31:06.320 --> 00:31:08.560
because I think I don't really care enough

00:31:08.560 --> 00:31:10.220
to argue with you about it.

00:31:10.360 --> 00:31:14.360
But I think they did a fine job with the yo-yo.

00:31:14.620 --> 00:31:15.920
And I actually think,

00:31:16.120 --> 00:31:17.760
if you can just get over

00:31:17.760 --> 00:31:19.900
maybe how simple it is

00:31:19.900 --> 00:31:22.440
compared to some of the other platformers

00:31:22.440 --> 00:31:23.300
we played this year,

00:31:23.460 --> 00:31:25.780
I think they made, or they re-skinned,

00:31:25.780 --> 00:31:27.500
a perfectly fine game.

00:31:27.880 --> 00:31:29.400
Yeah. You know, like,

00:31:29.480 --> 00:31:30.640
no, but I don't think, like,

00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:32.480
I don't think it ever gets

00:31:33.100 --> 00:31:33.960
the platforming part.

00:31:34.100 --> 00:31:35.600
The math pizza thing,

00:31:35.740 --> 00:31:37.760
like, whatever. But, like, the actual platforming levels,

00:31:38.440 --> 00:31:40.580
they're never boring, right?

00:31:40.660 --> 00:31:43.180
They're never just, like, tedious things that you have to do

00:31:43.180 --> 00:31:44.420
to get to the end of the stage

00:31:44.420 --> 00:31:46.000
or whatever. Like, they change it up enough.

00:31:46.200 --> 00:31:47.320
But it's also, like, never,

00:31:48.540 --> 00:31:49.900
the enemies are never like,

00:31:50.020 --> 00:31:51.320
oh, that was a cheap spawn,

00:31:51.320 --> 00:31:53.000
or, like, you know,

00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:54.840
oh, this guy takes a thousand hits

00:31:54.840 --> 00:31:55.720
with the yo-yo,

00:31:56.040 --> 00:31:58.500
like, what's the point? It moves at great pace.

00:31:58.500 --> 00:32:00.680
Well, I specifically did think that, but...

00:32:00.680 --> 00:32:03.300
Oh, for that one enemy, right?

00:32:04.300 --> 00:32:06.200
There's a couple that take some hits, right?

00:32:06.600 --> 00:32:08.660
Okay. No, there are definitely enemies

00:32:08.660 --> 00:32:09.760
that take multiple hits.

00:32:09.760 --> 00:32:11.080
Not everything is a one-hit KO,

00:32:11.240 --> 00:32:13.320
but I meant, like, I don't think there are, like,

00:32:13.960 --> 00:32:15.160
sponges in this game

00:32:15.160 --> 00:32:17.160
other than, like, there was that one enemy

00:32:17.160 --> 00:32:18.400
in the piers that I'm thinking of

00:32:18.400 --> 00:32:19.220
that, like, you had to hit, like,

00:32:19.220 --> 00:32:21.860
20 times. You also have some, like,

00:32:22.420 --> 00:32:24.040
mustachioed gentlemen that are kind of annoying,

00:32:24.100 --> 00:32:25.080
but I...

00:32:25.660 --> 00:32:27.400
Yeah, I did think

00:32:27.400 --> 00:32:28.600
that a lot of it was fine,

00:32:28.620 --> 00:32:29.660
but I think this is...

00:32:29.660 --> 00:32:30.620
This might be getting into

00:32:30.620 --> 00:32:32.160
some, like, essential game stuff,

00:32:32.300 --> 00:32:33.380
you know? Yeah, yeah, sure.

00:32:33.440 --> 00:32:34.760
I hear you. I guess I just...

00:32:34.760 --> 00:32:36.460
I don't want to... Because I'm complaining

00:32:36.460 --> 00:32:37.700
so much about the character,

00:32:38.200 --> 00:32:39.600
I didn't want to make it seem

00:32:39.600 --> 00:32:41.720
like the platforming here,

00:32:41.940 --> 00:32:43.420
like, control-wise,

00:32:44.040 --> 00:32:44.840
pacing-wise,

00:32:45.920 --> 00:32:46.860
content-wise, right?

00:32:46.900 --> 00:32:48.960
Just even from, like, the amount of stages,

00:32:49.220 --> 00:32:50.720
like, there's a good amount

00:32:51.260 --> 00:32:52.440
of stages here.

00:32:52.480 --> 00:32:53.400
It doesn't, like...

00:32:53.400 --> 00:32:55.180
It doesn't, like, take you to the pier

00:32:55.180 --> 00:32:56.300
and then you do, like,

00:32:56.880 --> 00:32:58.660
five levels of water

00:32:58.660 --> 00:33:00.260
back to back to back to...

00:33:00.260 --> 00:33:01.640
Yeah, agree. And then get out of there.

00:33:01.840 --> 00:33:03.360
Right. All right, Sean,

00:33:03.400 --> 00:33:04.660
now that the pizza's delivered,

00:33:05.300 --> 00:33:07.060
slice it or skip it

00:33:07.060 --> 00:33:08.820
on the Essential Games list.

00:33:12.560 --> 00:33:16.640
Yo! I'm annoyed by this game.

00:33:17.240 --> 00:33:18.620
I needed to qualify

00:33:18.620 --> 00:33:20.720
that it was...

00:33:20.720 --> 00:33:22.700
It was a good platformer,

00:33:22.720 --> 00:33:24.320
all things considered. I probably would like

00:33:24.320 --> 00:33:25.700
the Ninja game

00:33:25.700 --> 00:33:26.580
more than this.

00:33:28.120 --> 00:33:30.200
I guess what really

00:33:30.200 --> 00:33:31.120
annoys me about this game

00:33:31.120 --> 00:33:32.340
is just from a branding

00:33:32.340 --> 00:33:34.380
perspective. Like, there's...

00:33:34.860 --> 00:33:36.660
They're not eating a Domino's pizza.

00:33:36.980 --> 00:33:38.580
The Noid doesn't like pizza.

00:33:38.800 --> 00:33:39.700
On the very box,

00:33:39.720 --> 00:33:41.060
he has a pizza crusher

00:33:41.060 --> 00:33:42.300
that he's using as his, like,

00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:44.860
pogo stick. This is all just, like,

00:33:44.940 --> 00:33:47.080
a identity crisis

00:33:47.080 --> 00:33:48.580
for, like, who wants this?

00:33:48.580 --> 00:33:49.580
Because the consumer

00:33:49.580 --> 00:33:50.480
probably doesn't want

00:33:50.480 --> 00:33:52.040
to play as the Noid.

00:33:52.100 --> 00:33:53.880
That's not, like, one of my dream characters.

00:33:54.880 --> 00:33:56.640
You know, like, get the Noid in Smash?

00:33:56.820 --> 00:33:58.960
Like, no. But then, like,

00:33:58.960 --> 00:34:00.580
at the same time, it's not, like,

00:34:00.600 --> 00:34:02.760
an offensively bad game

00:34:03.200 --> 00:34:06.300
otherwise. So, I really just

00:34:06.300 --> 00:34:07.740
think that, like,

00:34:08.470 --> 00:34:09.700
it's just a really

00:34:09.700 --> 00:34:10.820
crazy decision

00:34:10.820 --> 00:34:12.400
by Capcom and Domino's

00:34:12.400 --> 00:34:14.020
to have these worlds meet.

00:34:14.180 --> 00:34:15.560
But I guess anything was possible

00:34:15.560 --> 00:34:16.720
in terms of crossovers

00:34:16.720 --> 00:34:18.020
in the 90s.

00:34:18.160 --> 00:34:19.560
So, it happened,

00:34:19.620 --> 00:34:21.080
but I don't think

00:34:21.080 --> 00:34:21.940
it should have happened.

00:34:22.360 --> 00:34:24.420
Sean? Yeah, we are all

00:34:24.420 --> 00:34:25.920
Kenneth Noid today.

00:34:27.020 --> 00:34:28.020
I don't think

00:34:28.020 --> 00:34:29.600
that this is a particularly good game.

00:34:29.600 --> 00:34:30.540
I don't even really

00:34:30.540 --> 00:34:31.780
have the same kind of

00:34:34.680 --> 00:34:35.840
good qualities

00:34:35.840 --> 00:34:40.020
that you're giving to the platforming parts.

00:34:40.020 --> 00:34:40.980
I think it's fine.

00:34:41.300 --> 00:34:43.400
But I think, like,

00:34:43.500 --> 00:34:44.340
this game

00:34:44.340 --> 00:34:46.420
had more value to me

00:34:46.420 --> 00:34:48.340
as that cultural object

00:34:48.340 --> 00:34:50.140
that we spent so much time talking about.

00:34:50.320 --> 00:34:52.060
I didn't even know what Noid was.

00:34:52.220 --> 00:34:53.800
I didn't know that crazy story

00:34:53.800 --> 00:34:56.660
about the stick-up.

00:34:57.340 --> 00:34:58.520
It's pretty crazy.

00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:00.220
I'll remember that.

00:35:00.780 --> 00:35:02.800
That's some fun fact stuff.

00:35:03.140 --> 00:35:04.420
But the game itself

00:35:04.420 --> 00:35:06.440
is almost wholly unremarkable.

00:35:06.760 --> 00:35:08.040
So, not essential.

00:35:08.660 --> 00:35:09.700
And Sean, just real fast

00:35:09.700 --> 00:35:11.200
before we end the episode,

00:35:11.440 --> 00:35:13.000
your go-to topping

00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:16.020
on a pizza? I'm a pretty standard

00:35:16.020 --> 00:35:19.180
pepperoni boy. I was pepperoni

00:35:19.180 --> 00:35:20.040
for so long

00:35:20.040 --> 00:35:21.220
and now I think

00:35:21.220 --> 00:35:22.160
I'm buffalo chicken.

00:35:22.460 --> 00:35:23.680
I think I want a little...

00:35:23.680 --> 00:35:24.540
Well, sure.

00:35:24.800 --> 00:35:26.780
If you're going for a specialty slice...

00:35:26.780 --> 00:35:28.100
Right, right. But I'm saying that's exclusively

00:35:28.100 --> 00:35:29.320
what I'm doing these days.

00:35:29.320 --> 00:35:30.800
I'm not ordering pies.

00:35:31.180 --> 00:35:32.200
Wow. All right.

00:35:32.480 --> 00:35:33.300
I'm going

00:35:33.300 --> 00:35:34.560
specialty slice,

00:35:34.560 --> 00:35:35.360
probably two,

00:35:35.860 --> 00:35:37.460
but two specialty slices,

00:35:37.520 --> 00:35:39.100
which is now a crazy price.

00:35:39.780 --> 00:35:40.740
It used to be

00:35:40.740 --> 00:35:42.760
$4 for a specialty slice

00:35:42.760 --> 00:35:44.180
and I feel like it's $8 now.

00:35:44.780 --> 00:35:47.360
Wow. But that's a good dinner.

00:35:47.560 --> 00:35:48.520
I don't want

00:35:48.520 --> 00:35:49.420
to order a pie

00:35:49.420 --> 00:35:51.000
and get eight slices

00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:51.920
when...

00:35:51.920 --> 00:35:52.980
I'm not in that

00:35:52.980 --> 00:35:54.080
sweet spot yet

00:35:54.080 --> 00:35:55.420
where I'm like a family of four.

00:35:55.720 --> 00:35:56.900
That's like the sweet spot

00:35:56.900 --> 00:35:58.460
for a pie. You definitely

00:35:59.360 --> 00:36:01.980
need company over to order a pie.

00:36:02.100 --> 00:36:04.140
But I do also do the specialty slice thing,

00:36:04.320 --> 00:36:05.280
but I do one

00:36:05.280 --> 00:36:06.240
specialty slice

00:36:06.760 --> 00:36:09.080
and one pepperoni slice.

00:36:09.240 --> 00:36:11.300
All right. So if we're going like normal slices

00:36:11.300 --> 00:36:12.200
because buffalo chicken

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:13.920
is a little out there, I would say

00:36:13.920 --> 00:36:14.780
I agree with you

00:36:14.780 --> 00:36:16.660
with the pepperoni, but people are sleeping

00:36:16.660 --> 00:36:18.840
on meatball. I like meatball.

00:36:19.040 --> 00:36:20.380
Yeah, that's fun. I think people are sleeping

00:36:20.380 --> 00:36:22.580
on it, you know? And especially

00:36:22.580 --> 00:36:23.500
if the meatball

00:36:23.500 --> 00:36:24.300
is actually

00:36:25.240 --> 00:36:26.340
baked on there

00:36:26.340 --> 00:36:27.320
at the same time,

00:36:27.360 --> 00:36:28.480
like it's made as a slice,

00:36:28.480 --> 00:36:30.080
not like, oh, we made a cheese pizza

00:36:30.080 --> 00:36:31.340
and then we added some meatballs

00:36:31.340 --> 00:36:32.200
that we cooked. Yeah.

00:36:32.320 --> 00:36:34.160
No, it's all got to be

00:36:34.160 --> 00:36:36.140
in harmony. Which in the same vein,

00:36:36.820 --> 00:36:37.840
if you're going to go

00:36:37.840 --> 00:36:39.100
for a specialty slice

00:36:39.100 --> 00:36:40.360
and you're really

00:36:40.360 --> 00:36:41.400
trying to carbo-load,

00:36:42.560 --> 00:36:44.020
put some panne on there.

00:36:44.680 --> 00:36:45.700
There's nothing better

00:36:45.700 --> 00:36:46.740
in some instances

00:36:46.740 --> 00:36:48.380
than just some pasta

00:36:48.380 --> 00:36:50.440
in a pie. And should anybody

00:36:50.440 --> 00:36:53.420
want to know, my favorite New York slice

00:36:53.420 --> 00:36:55.300
is Sal and Carmine's Pizza

00:36:55.300 --> 00:36:56.860
on 104th Street

00:36:56.860 --> 00:36:59.180
and Broadway. I think that

00:36:59.760 --> 00:37:00.960
you get a cheese slice

00:37:00.960 --> 00:37:02.740
from there, it basically tastes like

00:37:02.740 --> 00:37:03.740
how you imagine

00:37:03.740 --> 00:37:05.260
pizza tasted when you were like

00:37:05.260 --> 00:37:06.120
six or seven

00:37:06.120 --> 00:37:07.300
and just went nuts for it.

00:37:07.600 --> 00:37:08.480
That's what it's like

00:37:08.480 --> 00:37:09.940
for me. Sean, I don't mean

00:37:09.940 --> 00:37:11.780
to put you on the spot, but do you have a go-to?

00:37:12.900 --> 00:37:13.760
I prefer

00:37:13.760 --> 00:37:14.860
Buffalo-style pizza.

00:37:15.360 --> 00:37:39.340
Woof. Woof.!!!!!!!!!!! Bye.
